# `vite --mode mock` (npm run dev:mock) only. Vite loads .env.[mode] after
# .env and .env.local, so these WIN over a real project's values while mock
# mode is running and are invisible to every other command.
#
# NOTHING SECRET IS HERE, and nothing can be: the file is tracked precisely so
# that `npm run dev:mock` needs no setup, and both values are fakes.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL is a RELATIVE path, which is what makes this work. The app's
# lib/account.ts builds `${VITE_SUPABASE_URL}/auth/v1/otp` and hands it to
# fetch, so a relative base resolves against the dev server's own origin and
# lands on the GoTrue routes in dev/mockApi.ts. The production code has no idea
# mock mode exists and needs no branch for it.
#
# ONE KNOWN COST: /admin.html reads the same two variables
# (src/panik-admin/lib/supabaseAuth.ts), so the admin console cannot sign in
# while the dev server is in mock mode. Run `npm run dev` for that surface.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=/mock-supabase
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=mock-publishable-key
